WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.204
Canada has a long history of leadership

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:04.904
in the development

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.473
of artificial intelligence

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.540
dating right back

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.309
to CIFAR’s very first program

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.677
in the 1980's.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:11.978
Canada's leadership in

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.179
AI continues today

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.180
at the three

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.882
National AI Institutes created

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.284
through the Pan-Canadian AI Strategy.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:18.918
Six years

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.387
into the launch of the Strategy,

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.956
we've named over 120 world-leading

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:26.426
researchers as Canada CIFAR AI Chairs.

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:29.062
In turn, they train thousands of students,

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.096
expanding Canada's

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.532
pool of AI talent every year.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.333
As a result,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.268
Canada is leading the world for

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.971
AI research, consistently producing more

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:38.605
AI-related

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.707
research publications per capita

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.342
than any G7 nation,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.411
and tripling our research productivity

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.246
since the start of the Strategy.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.615
But the impact of the Pan-Canadian

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.983
AI Strategy goes way

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.751
beyond research excellence.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.520
The Strategy is delivering

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.155
significant social

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:58.458
and economic benefits for all of Canada.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.626
For example,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.860
the number of jobs in

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.695
AI has grown significantly.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:06.066
More than 140,000 AI professionals

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.635
were working in Canada by 2022.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.171
This number increased by 29%

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.105
in a single year,

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.206
which is remarkable

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.641
growth in today's economy.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.508
And Canada

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.676
has more than doubled

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.044
the number of AI startups

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.213
since the launch of the strategy.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.448
These are new companies

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.550
that are commercializing innovative,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.085
AI-based products and services

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.387
to improve our lives and economy.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.289
But it is crucial

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.224
that we get the future of AI right

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.559
and that we deploy

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.861
and regulate it responsibly.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.029
Canada's leadership in responsible

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.764
AI development and regulation

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.998
will drive innovation

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.366
and economic productivity,

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.068
while at the same time

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:42.936
helping to address

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.771
some of the most challenging problems

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.972
facing humanity

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:49.509
through these made-in-Canada advances.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.844
All this means

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.113
that it is truly the time

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.714
for Canada to shine.

